The weight of a snake is defined as thickness $\times$ length.
We are given $N$ snakes. For the $i$-th snake, the initial thickness is $T_i$ and the initial length is $L_i$.
For a specific $k$, the new length of the $i$-th snake becomes $L_i + k$.
The new weight of the $i$-th snake is $T_i \times (L_i + k)$.
We need to find $\max_{i} (T_i \times (L_i + k))$ for each $k \in \{1, \dots, D\}$.

